### Test 5: International Order
POST {{web_api_base}}/api/demo/fulfillment/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-2026-005",
  "customerName": "Carlos Rodriguez",
  "customerEmail": "CARLOS.RODRIGUEZ@EXAMPLE.MX",
  "orderDate": "2026-01-10T18:00:00Z",
  "totalAmount": 799.99,
  "currency": "USD",
  "items": [
    {
      "sku": "tablet-ipad",
      "productName": "iPad Air 5th Generation",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 799.99
    }
  ],
  "shippingAddress": {
    "street": "Av. Insurgentes Sur 1234",
    "city": "Mexico City",
    "state": "CDMX",
    "postalCode": "03100",
    "country": "MEX"
  },
  "priority": "EXPRESS"
}

### ============================================
### Expected Transformations to Verify
### ============================================

# After sending requests above, check:
#
# 1. Email ToLower transformer:
#    - JOHN.SMITH@EXAMPLE.COM → john.smith@example.com
#    - Jane.Doe@Example.COM → jane.doe@example.com
#    - BOB@EXAMPLE.COM → bob@example.com
#
# 2. SKU ToUpper transformer:
#    - laptop-xps15 → LAPTOP-XPS15
#    - phone-iphone15 → PHONE-IPHONE15
#    - workstation-dell → WORKSTATION-DELL
#
# 3. Priority MapValue transformer:
#    - STANDARD → STD
#    - EXPRESS → EXP
#    - OVERNIGHT → OVN
#
# 4. Array mappings:
#    - Each item in items[] creates a LineItems/Item element
#    - Multi-item order creates multiple <Item> nodes

### ============================================
### Test SOAP to JSON Integration
### ============================================

### Test SOAP to JSON Status Response
POST {{web_api_base}}/api/demo/fulfillment/status
Content-Type: text/xml

<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
  <soap:Body>
    <FulfillmentStatusResponse>
      <OrderNumber>ORD-2026-001</OrderNumber>
      <Status>SHIPPED</Status>
      <TrackingNumber>1Z999AA10123456784</TrackingNumber>
      <EstimatedDelivery>2026-01-15T00:00:00Z</EstimatedDelivery>
      <LastUpdated>2026-01-10T16:45:00Z</LastUpdated>
    </FulfillmentStatusResponse>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>

### Expected JSON Output:
# {
#   "orderId": "ORD-2026-001",
#   "status": "shipped",
#   "trackingNumber": "1Z999AA10123456784",
#   "estimatedDeliveryDate": "2026-01-15T00:00:00Z",
#   "lastUpdated": "2026-01-10T16:45:00Z"
# }

### ============================================
### Health Checks
### ============================================

### Check Management API health
GET {{management_api_base}}/health

### Check QuickApiMapper Web health
GET {{web_api_base}}/health

### ============================================
### Cleanup / Reset Demo Data
### ============================================

### Delete a demo integration (replace ID with actual ID from GET call)
# DELETE {{management_api_base}}/api/integrations/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### To force re-seed:
# 1. Set ForceReseed to true in appsettings.Development.json
# 2. Restart the Management API
# 3. Set ForceReseed back to false
